        "parms": "# ~lp and ~hp — lowpass and highpass\nA ~lp lets the frequencies below its cutoff through and turns down those above; a ~hp does the opposite. Both are single-pole filters with a gentle slope, 6 dB per octave. The argument is the cutoff in Hz, and a float on the right inlet changes it.\nMax builds these with onepole~ or biquad~, which take the cutoff as a signal or a number. Here the cutoff is a number, and only a float: an int is ignored.",
